"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1010-08-15:0":{"b": ["Valencia passed into the hands of the Amirid freedmen Mubarak and Muzaffar", "38ac8e22"], "d": ["With the dissolution of the power of the grandsons of the hajib Mansur, Valencia came under the rule of the Amirid freedmen Mubarak and Muzaffar; taifa emirates began to appear in al-Andalus.", "82f013cc"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1013-01-01:0":{"b": ["Sulayman al-Musta'in and his supporters entered Cordoba and deposed Hisham II again; at least sixty scholars were killed in the city (403/1013; the source gives the year, no day).", "e863c0b4"], "d": ["Sulayman al-Musta'in and his supporters entered Cordoba and deposed Hisham II again; at least sixty scholars were killed in the city (403/1013; the source gives the year, no day).", "e863c0b4"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1016-01-01:0":{"b": ["The Hammudids seized Cordoba and the throne of al-Andalus", "a8a8ea65"], "d": ["The Shi'i Hammudids, who claimed descent from Ali, took advantage of the impotence of the Umayyad dynasty to seize Cordoba and the throne of the caliphate in 1016; Cordoba remained under their rule between 1016 and 1022.", "b088ab2a"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1021-01-01:0":{"b": ["The Amirid dynasty was founded with Valencia as its centre (1021-1094)", "ebf0b6e2"], "d": ["Abd al-Aziz b. Abd al-Rahman, a grandson of the hajib al-Mansur, founded in 1021 the Amirid taifa emirate whose centre was Valencia; the dynasty lasted, with some interruptions, until 1094.", "dc1ccee5"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1023-03-26:0":{"b": ["The qadi Ibn Abbad declared Seville the seat of government (Abbadids)", "931db55e"], "d": ["The qadi Abu'l-Qasim Ibn Abbad declared Seville the seat of government in 414 (1023); the Abbadid taifa emirate became one of the most important centres of al-Andalus.", "51e3b6d5"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1031-01-01:0":{"b": ["Cordoba became a republic under the Jahwarids (1031-1070)", "943bc77c"], "d": ["After the end of the Umayyad dynasty, Cordoba became a republic under the rule of the Jahwarids from 1031 to 1070.", "6afd1a28"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1049-06-05:0":{"b": ["When the Fatimid vizier al-Yazuri appointed the chief of the Zughba as emir of Tripoli and Gabès, the Banu Hilal turned westward (441, 1049).", "481a1144"], "d": ["When the Fatimid vizier al-Yazuri appointed the chief of the Zughba as emir of Tripoli and Gabès, the Banu Hilal turned westward (441, 1049).", "481a1144"]},
