"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1070-01-01:0":{"b": ["Cordoba passed to the Abbadids after the Jahwarids", "fc156474"], "d": ["Jahwarid rule lasted until 1070; Cordoba then passed into the hands of the Abbadid emirate centred on Seville.", "d8bc19d6"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1080-01-01:0":{"b": ["The Almoravids took Tlemcen, Oujda and Oran and reached the city of Algiers", "cefef422"], "d": ["Yusuf b. Tashfin turned toward the Central Maghrib, took Oujda, Tlemcen and Oran, and reached the city of Algiers (1080); in Algiers he had the Great Mosque built.", "8bfdcd25"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1086-06-30:0":{"b": ["Yusuf b. Tashfin landed at Algeciras; the first crossing to al-Andalus", "ad79ab8b"], "d": ["At the invitation of thirteen Andalusian emirs, Yusuf landed on the coast on 15 Rabi I 479 (30 June 1086), on condition that Algeciras be given to him, and crossed to Seville.", "77396cfd"]},
"OLAYLAR_ORTACAG_IBERYA_MAGRIB:1086-10-23:0":{"b": ["Yusuf b. Tashfin defeated the Castilian army at Zallaqa (12 Rajab 479).", "7f7d340d"], "d": ["Yusuf b. Tashfin defeated the Castilian army at Zallaqa (12 Rajab 479).", "7f7d340d"]},
